{"title":"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 78","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_78&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Feeling excited over her successful explorations into Pascal's Triangle, Wendy formulates a second problem to use during a future Jupiter Falls High School Math Meet:\n</p><p><i>How many of the first 2010 rows of Pascal's Triangle (Rows 0 through 2009) have exactly 256 odd entries?</i>\n</p><p>What is the solution to Wendy's second problem? \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_78&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Building off of Method 2 in problem 77, we see that each that the base 2 representation of the number reveals to us how many times we end up applying the\nrecursion relation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/255783c10f64d99ab4639a8fb7f0410a5fdda61c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_k=2*O_{k-2^{n-1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"132\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/8/e6825f51aabbbbf1ca2d2954d5511f3ca58b62e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2008=1024+512+256+128+64+16+8=(11111011000)_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"501\" height=\"18\" /> has seven nonzero terms in its base 2 expansion so that we end up\napplying the recursion relation seven times giving a final term of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/6/676c3198f8cfe4924133e4d4e65c03923e4871d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_{2008}=2^7\\cdot O_{0}=2^7=128$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"208\" height=\"17\" />. So we need to count the number of integers between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/9/d59b22c70df3b6d4a4b90727aec5f10cd243bcc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{0,2009\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> which\nhave exactly 8 nonzero terms in their base 2 expansion. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/3/6f30d96abff2bfd2b1573afe6cdfdf490d835d31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2009=(11111011001)_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"180\" height=\"18\" />.  \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/c/26cd8b03df9811f1d6f981785a8159e58c03dc67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{11}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"42\" height=\"53\" /> counts the numbers up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/a/74ad308bd43845875f11d9b9b8520305ffbdd228.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2047=2^{11}-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"114\" height=\"15\" /> which have exactly 8 nonzero terms\nin their base 2 expansion. Of these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/9/8392b5820acb45b5afea3c4a56473be63d1d1057.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{11}{8}=165$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"97\" height=\"53\" /> candidates, the following 12 must be excluded since they exceed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/7/85727a3ea4f5d7ba25bc591590b0e085bca557b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2009$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/3/cf3f87fd69bb232a3899ea1766047113634b6c2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2040=(11111111000)_2,2036(11111110100)_2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"352\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/e/5cea2ee8e9db0861d8c7719553304dd1df274e51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2034=(11111110010)_2,2033=(11111110001)_2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"376\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/c/c9c19763749918941ce2b04720cd7d2427fd3370.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2028=(11111101100)_2,2026=(11111101010)_2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"376\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/a/36a25795b2202eb747cd5a0ea73dcfb47fe86819.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025=(11111101001)_2,2022=(11111100110)_2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"376\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/f/87ffd14540c5ffcede70e057964cc83271b53ff8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2021=(11111100101)_2,2019=(11111100011)_2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"376\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/7/8b7dc780c77ca1cf21aff88da2d29b2d24a638e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2012=(11111011100)_2,2010=(1111011010)_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"361\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>This gives an answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/8/098182308be7edd7a7583a308478cd45ce2d0995.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$165-12=153$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"118\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_78&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By Lucas' Theorem, we require there to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ones in the binary representation of the row number. Continue as in solution 1.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_78&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest\" title=\"2008 iTest\">2008 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems\">(Problems)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_77\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 77\">Problem 77</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_79\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 79\">Problem 79</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Pr